548	{"artifactId":"LLD-c66d49bb81925886-s1","entry":{"id":"591c16e7ac0e4975a53f8ecb4d7fe1dc","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:26:24.613Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"f7d737c27a71ea38bc20595f54c5be9ac6b89c008535cb32cdb045c0f337a2da"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Pre-review packaging refinement: statically imported .avsc.json/logical schemas and compiled-output smoke qualification; preserve pure runtime APIs and sibling scope."},"addresses":"all"}}
10302	{"artifactId":"LLD-c66d49bb81925886-s1","entry":{"id":"review-baf18193b89930fe746c8b19554c886f","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:26:39.725Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the six upstream s1 acceptance criteria without introducing runtime capture, persistence or hierarchy reporting.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 requires attempt identity, counter quality, non-overlapping corrections, reference conflicts, effective ownership and capability distinctions. LLD §§2–3 and its six-row acceptance mapping address each; filesystem writing and TU2/TU3 capture remain excluded. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Retain these scope boundaries during implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing provider response shapes do not establish complete native usage visibility.","evidence":"LLMResponse declares optional usage with required inputTokens/outputTokens and optional cache fields. Ollama's stream loop captures numeric counters only on done chunks and returns usage only when both counts exist. CliProvider.complete returns text and stopReason for both CLI paths without usage. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Preserve unknown capability and missing-counter states in the proposed survey.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing compiler and asset packaging support the proposed static JSON-module distribution approach.","evidence":"tsconfig.json sets module/moduleResolution to nodenext and resolveJsonModule=true. copy-assets.mjs copies only ['prompts', 'assets']; package.json uses ESM and requires Node >=22.13.0. The design correctly requires production imports and a compiled-output smoke test rather than assuming arbitrary schema directories are copied. [files: tsconfig.json, copy-assets.mjs, package.json]","action":"Run the proposed built-output schema/digest test during implementation; this review does not establish that future modules already load.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactIds and the two existing canonicalization domains are appropriate reuse boundaries.","evidence":"ArtifactIds.parse validates strict kind/hash/story/task shapes; parentOf handles TASK/TASKS/DIAG→STORY and STORY→EPIC only. Lifecycle canonicalJson is private and deliberately uses JSON.stringify persisted semantics, including toJSON and dropped undefined. Design-corpus canonicalJson independently inspects descriptors and rejects accessors, cycles and sparse arrays. A separate strict usage canonicalizer avoids changing either existing contract. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"Reuse ArtifactIds syntax while keeping usage hashing separate from contentHash and corpus errors/limits.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed public API preserves the HLD sc1/sc2 signatures and identifies an additive implementation boundary.","evidence":"HLD §5.1 defines validate(record), reduce(AsyncIterable, scope), decimal-string totals and string notices; §5.2 defines UsageBinding, BindingRequest, BindingResolution and UsageAttributionPolicy. The LLD preserves these signatures and explicitly proposes new usage modules rather than modifying provider or artifact identity APIs. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Keep typed internal refinements assignable to these HLD interfaces.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The ER companion accurately expresses predecessor cardinality for original and corrected observations.","evidence":"The companion defines UsageObservation as 'A terminal or corrected observation' but emits 'UsageObservation ||--o{ UsageObservation : \"successorCorrections\"'. This requires exactly one predecessor for every observation, including original terminal observations. The LLD requires a predecessor for corrections, not for original finishes. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/er-model.html]","action":"Have the author correct the structured relationship definition to permit original observations without predecessors and regenerate the companion, retaining the documented fork-conflict rule.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generated ER companion renders correctly and remains visually consistent with the design.","evidence":"Inspected the embedded Mermaid, relationship descriptions and rendering bootstrap. Attempted to open the local companion through the in-app browser; the tool returned 'Browser is not available: iab'. Mermaid execution, layout and clipping were not visually verified. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/er-model.html]","action":"Render the regenerated companion in an available browser and inspect its layout and relationship labels.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The additive rollout preserves existing artifact content and distinguishes historical absence from measured zero.","evidence":"HLD requires independent Avro facts, unchanged artifact content hashes and explicit legacy/missing states. Existing contentHash hashes only description, body and citations. The LLD introduces separate domain exports, prohibits artifact rewrites/backfill and retains legacy/missing/unsupported accounting states. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Keep future persisted-schema migrations and storage activation with the owning sibling stories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The transfer rules preserve the HLD distinction between same-root reassignment and cross-root transfer.","evidence":"HLD §3 explicitly states: 'Same-root reassignment uses one committed control operation.' LLD §3.3 instead requires transfers to follow prepared→accepted→committed references and says only matching committed pairs change ownership, without defining a same-root exception or its single-operation payload. Implementing that rule would reject valid HLD same-root reassignments. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Specify the same-root committed-operation shape and reducer semantics separately from cross-root closure; align the shared contract and add a positive single-operation same-root fixture.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Malformed, ambiguous, incomplete and interrupted accounting inputs have explicit non-zero-fabricating outcomes.","evidence":"Against the HLD's identity-conflict, missing-reference, pending and unsupported requirements, the LLD specifies bounded validation notices, exclusion of ambiguous contributions, closure checks and rejection on resource/iterator failure. It explicitly prohibits treating rejection or unavailable counters as zero and retains counters from failed calls. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement and test these stated outcomes; resolve the separate same-root transfer mismatch before building.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s1 acceptance criterion maps to concrete proposed tests using the repository's existing test conventions.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.1 ac1–ac6 and the HLD acceptance matrix with LLD §7: each maps to named identity/attribution, validation/arithmetic, reconciliation, conflict/closure, transfer or capability fixtures. Existing internal-retry.test.ts uses node:test, node:assert/strict and fake CLI/Ollama inputs; package.json already supplies tsx and avsc. These are planned tests, not claimed passing tests. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md, src/agent/providers/__tests__/internal-retry.test.ts, package.json]","action":"Retain the six-criterion mapping and add the explicit single-operation same-root transfer case required by the boundary correction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T11:26:39.725Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
