12023	{"artifactId":"LLD-c66d49bb81925886-s1","entry":{"id":"review-589007436789215a3d4d5f745173e909","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:50:30.918Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers s1's six acceptance criteria without implementing the upstream non-goals.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 requires attempt identity, counter quality, correction/overlap accounting, reference conflicts, effective ownership and source-capability distinctions. LLD §§3 and 7 address all six. DEF §3 excludes capture, host integration, subtree reporting, pricing and content-store replacement; the LLD leaves these outside s1. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing provider abstraction and Ollama implementation do not establish complete native usage visibility.","evidence":"LLMResponse declares optional usage with required inputTokens/outputTokens and optional cache fields. Ollama completeStreaming reads numeric counters only from done chunks and returns usage only when both promptEvalCount and evalCount are defined. CliProvider.complete returns text/stopReason without usage for both CLI branches. These bodies support retaining unknown coverage and avoiding cache-zero assumptions. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Preserve the planned distinction between application-visible counters and native completeness.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Usage canonicalization must remain separate from the existing artifact content hash and design-corpus canonicalizer.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts has a private canonicalJson that first uses JSON.stringify, including persisted toJSON behavior and dropping undefined; contentHash hashes description/body/citations. design/corpus/canonical.ts separately exports descriptor-based canonicalJson with CorpusInputError and corpus-specific limits. Neither is the proposed usage source identity contract. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed usage accounting APIs are new, while ArtifactIds is an appropriate existing syntax dependency.","evidence":"The analyzer returned no established accounting implementation and disclosed incomplete retrieval; direct source searches found no LedgerRecord, UsageReducer or UsageAttributionPolicy implementation. Existing workflow/attribution.ts handles model stamps and legacy labels, not charged ownership or counters. Reading ArtifactIds confirms strict parse/make support for the proposed root/document/task kinds and only limited parentOf relationships. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/attribution.ts]","action":"Reuse ArtifactIds parsing without treating parentOf or existing model attribution as root-resolution/accounting services.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed public methods and additive effective ownership result conform to the approved shared contracts.","evidence":"HLD §5 defines the same validate/reduce and attribution-policy signatures. The amendment file records lifecycle.status='approved' and fieldAdd sc1.effectiveOwners with the same optional array shape, including capture owner, effective owner/version, basis/provenance IDs and state. Its purpose explicitly requires new reducers to populate it and grouping consumers to reject absent attribution. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c66d49bb81925886-1.json]","action":"Retain the amendment's result-field placement and compatibility rules.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The schema distribution plan accounts for the actual production build configuration.","evidence":"tsconfig.json uses NodeNext, resolveJsonModule=true and outDir=out, excluding tests. copy-assets.mjs copies only prompts and assets. package.json declares ESM, TypeScript ^5.9.0 and Node >=22.13.0. Static production JSON imports plus the planned compiled-output/digest smoke check address this configuration without assuming arbitrary resource copying. [files: tsconfig.json, copy-assets.mjs, package.json, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Execute the compiled-output smoke check during implementation; this review does not establish that the proposed modules already compile.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked ER companion renders consistently with the design.","evidence":"Read the actual HTML's Mermaid source and entity/relationship descriptions. It models AccountingGroup observations/reconciliations and UsageObservation successor correction facets, explaining multiplicity, predecessor ownership and non-additive projections. The remaining transfer/ownership relationships are specified in LLD prose. Rendering could not be inspected: the in-app browser was unavailable and Chrome's browser policy blocked the local file URL. No visual verification is claimed. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/er-model.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Have the author verify the existing companion rendering through an allowed local preview; regenerate if rendering is broken or inconsistent.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The additive rollout preserves existing artifact/provider data and treats historical usage absence explicitly.","evidence":"HLD §3 describes the usage ledger as proposed and independent of artifact JSON. The current contentHash body covers description/body/citations, and current provider usage remains optional. LLD §8 introduces separate exports without rewriting those records; missing history stays not-recorded, unsupported schemas remain explicit, and incompatible writer schemas cannot mix within a container. The approved ownership amendment is optional for base consumers. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/shared/types.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c66d49bb81925886-1.json]","action":"Keep the planned schema round-trip, absent-attribution and legacy-quality fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's transfer semantics, binding validation and schema ownership stay within s1's approved responsibilities.","evidence":"HLD §6.1 explicitly assigns pure correction/non-overlap/transfer state machines, physical Avro requirements and binding evidence to s1. §§6.2–6.4 assign root resolution/storage/indexes to s2, transfer coordination/import to s3 and daemon/query qualification to s4. The LLD evaluates supplied references and owner versions without implementing those sibling operations. HLD §3 also explicitly permits one committed control operation for same-root reassignment. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Identity, correction, overlap and transfer failures have explicit detection and conservative accounting outcomes.","evidence":"Against HLD's immutable-history and unresolved-conflict requirements, LLD §§3.2–3.3 and 6 specify canonical duplicate comparisons, second-start conflicts, missing/forked/cyclic references, stale reconciliation candidates and transfer version/closure validation. Ambiguous contributions are excluded with conflict/partial diagnostics rather than timestamp selection, copied counters or guessed residuals; pending transfers retain the committed owner. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Truncated evidence, malformed measurements and interrupted iteration cannot be interpreted as a complete zero.","evidence":"HLD distinguishes pending/unavailable/legacy from zero and requires bounded exact arithmetic. LLD §6 supplies detection and handling for unsafe counters, missing baselines, unsupported sources, event-set/count/digest mismatches and resource/iterator failures. The design requires rejection with no successful partial result for iterator/resource failure, while incomplete evidence produces explicit quality notices. It correctly limits pure descriptor checking to consistency rather than service authority. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s1 acceptance criterion maps to concrete planned tests using existing repository test conventions.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.1 and HLD's acceptance matrix with LLD §7: ac1 maps identity/attribution, ac2 counter quality/exact sums, ac3 correction/overlap/cumulative bases, ac4 identity/reference/closure conflicts, ac5 same-root and cross-root owner/provenance semantics, and ac6 source survey/schema fixtures. Additional proposed tests cover compiled schema distribution and amendment compatibility. Existing internal-retry.test.ts uses node:test, node:assert/strict and fake CLI/Ollama clients, supporting the stated fixture approach. Proposed tests are not claimed to exist or pass. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md, src/agent/providers/__tests__/internal-retry.test.ts, package.json]","action":"Implement and run the mapped fixtures; retain explicit unknown/unqualified source cases rather than requiring live inference.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T11:50:30.918Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
