10669	{"artifactId":"LLD-c66d49bb81925886-s1","entry":{"id":"review-2465c1d34c4760536dfff2f2a378eca2","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:42:22.139Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the upstream s1 acceptance criteria without implementing excluded capture, persistence or reporting features.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 ac1–ac6 require distinct attempts/replay, counter quality, non-overlapping corrections, conflict detection, traceable ownership and qualified source capabilities. LLD §§3.1–3.6 design each obligation; its exclusions match HLD §6.1: 'no filesystem writer, provider capture or hierarchy totals.' [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Retain these scope limits during implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The implementation is a partial foundation, rather than an existing runtime ledger or reducer.","evidence":"Git history contains the cited t1/t2/t3 commits. The usage directory contains types, schemas, canonicalization and foundation tests. index.ts states 'Complete runtime implementations are published in task t11' and exports only types. Searches found no implemented UsageReducer or UsageAttributionPolicy elsewhere. The analyzer did not return a bundle; direct reads and repository searches supplied the evidence. [files: src/workflow/usage/types.ts, src/workflow/usage/index.ts, src/workflow/usage/schemas.ts, src/workflow/usage/canonical.ts]","action":"Extend these foundations as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing provider usage fields do not establish complete native-call or cache coverage.","evidence":"LLMResponse declares optional usage with required inputTokens/outputTokens and optional cache fields. Ollama reads numeric counters only from done chunks and emits usage only when both counts exist. CliProvider.complete and runEditSession return text/stopReason without usage. These implementations support the design's conservative capability qualification. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Record these exact source limitations in the proposed survey.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactIds and canonicalization are reused or separated according to their actual responsibilities.","evidence":"ArtifactIds.parse validates canonical kind/hash/story/task forms; parentOf handles only TASK/TASKS/DIAG→STORY and STORY→EPIC. Lifecycle canonicalJson is private and hashes persisted JSON semantics, including toJSON; design-corpus canonicalJson has separate CorpusInputError/CORPUS_LIMITS. Existing usage canonical.ts independently inspects descriptors and computes the domain-separated source digest. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/design/corpus/canonical.ts, src/workflow/usage/canonical.ts]","action":"Keep root resolution outside ArtifactIds and preserve the independent content-hash contracts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed API and schema distribution changes target the existing contracts and production build mechanism.","evidence":"types.ts already carries the stated reducer and attribution signatures. schemas.ts statically imports both JSON schemas with import attributes and freezes them. tsconfig enables NodeNext and resolveJsonModule; copy-assets.mjs copies only prompts/assets. The proposed runtime barrel and compiled schema smoke test therefore address the actual publication gap. [files: src/workflow/usage/types.ts, src/workflow/usage/schemas.ts, src/workflow/usage/index.ts, tsconfig.json, copy-assets.mjs]","action":"Complete the barrel and compiled-output qualification before publishing the runtime contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Relationship documentation is adequate for the proposed pure accounting model.","evidence":"The ER source documents group-to-observation/reconciliation cardinalities and correction successors. LLD prose supplies the material additional rules: one effective correction successor, complete reconciliation candidates, immutable capture ownership, versioned same-root reassignment and cross-root phase references. Compatibility is explicitly described. Together these specify endpoints, direction and ownership without requiring another diagram. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/er-model.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Optionally expand the companion to illustrate transfer provenance; the prose already supplies the necessary relationship contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked ER companion renders correctly.","evidence":"Inspected the embedded Mermaid source and rendering/bootstrap code. Attempted to open the local companion through the in-app browser, which returned 'Browser is not available: iab'. Actual Mermaid execution, layout and clipping could not be verified. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/er-model.html]","action":"Render the existing companion in an available browser and inspect its layout and consistency.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design preserves existing artifact/provider data and adopts effective ownership through an approved additive contract.","evidence":"AMD-c66d49bb81925886-1 has lifecycle status 'approved' and adds optional effectiveOwners to EffectiveAccounting, explicitly requiring new reducers to populate it and consumers to treat absence as unavailable. types.ts implements that optional result field. The logical/Avro schemas preserve nullable counters and typed transfer modes; migration introduces no content rewrite or historical usage backfill. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c66d49bb81925886-1.json, src/workflow/usage/types.ts, src/workflow/usage/ledger-record.v1.schema.json, src/workflow/usage/ledger-record.v1.avsc.json]","action":"Preserve optional-field compatibility and qualify readers before later persistence activation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design respects HLD story ownership and shared signatures.","evidence":"HLD §§5–6 assign normalized events/reduction and binding evidence to s1, durable root/snapshot services to s2, transfer coordination to s3 and daemon/query qualification to s4. The LLD limits itself to supplied-evidence validation and pure owner-state evaluation, preserving the sc1/sc2 method signatures and leaving authority, IO and capture outside this story. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, src/workflow/usage/types.ts]","action":"Keep completeness-descriptor construction and authority checks in the owning service stories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design states detectable failure conditions and prevents failures from becoming trusted zero or speculative ownership.","evidence":"LLD §6 specifies detection and handling for malformed data, digest/identity conflicts, invalid counters, reference forks/cycles, overlap, baselines, attribution, transfers, closure and resource/iterator failures. Existing canonical.ts supplies descriptor inspection, proxy/cycle rejection and bounded traversal; types.ts supplies resource-limit/source-unavailable errors and nullable unresolved owners. Runtime reduction is correctly identified as future implementation. [files: src/workflow/usage/canonical.ts, src/workflow/usage/types.ts, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the specified notices and rejection paths; do not treat the current canonicalizer as the complete validator.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s1 acceptance criterion maps to concrete proposed tests, with existing foundation tests accurately treated as partial coverage.","evidence":"Compared DEF ac1–ac6 with LLD §7: identity/attribution covers ac1; quality/exact arithmetic ac2; correction/reconciliation/cumulative intervals ac3; identity/reference/closure failures ac4; transfer-state/effectiveOwners ac5; capability survey/schema fixtures ac6. Existing identity tests exercise replay and adversarial traversal; schema-contract tests exercise compiler compatibility and in-memory Avro round trips. Neither currently proves the proposed reducer, attribution or capability runtime. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/usage/__tests__/identity.test.ts, src/workflow/usage/__tests__/schema-contract.test.ts]","action":"Implement the remaining mapped tests, including compiled-output schema loading, without presenting existing foundation tests as full acceptance.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T14:42:22.139Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
